From f9719b375078c55b98e247bb748d5d7d483202fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel FORTE <2580288+g4bwy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:58:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Perf][Spec Decode] Adaptive MTP draft depth from acceptance
 history

Fixed-depth MTP over-drafts whenever content is hard: on live traffic
the average step accepts 1.9 of 4 drafts (per-position survival
0.73/0.53/0.40/0.29), while synthetic repeat prompts pin near the
ceiling - the depth that pays off swings with content, not just batch
size.

Adopt the B12X acceptance-length controller (Apache-2.0, vendored
verbatim from local-inference-lab/vllm dev/karmic-kraken commit
8244d1c443; report in eugr/spark-vllm-docker#432, positive field data
on this model family and GLM-5.3-Flash). speculative-config gains
adaptive_speculative_tokens_window and adaptive_speculative_tokens_initial;
num_speculative_tokens stays the cap. Per window, the scheduler computes
target = clamp(floor(mean_accepted + 1.5), 1, cap), drops to target
immediately and climbs one token per window: fast back-off, slow
recovery, no oscillation. Controllers are per distinct batch-size cap
when combined with the existing num_speculative_tokens_per_batch_size
table.

Transport is upstream's (#57053): per-step num_spec_tokens_to_schedule,
-1-marked ungenerated drafts, per-K graph tiers. This patch adds the
scheduler wiring, the reachable-depth CUDA-graph tiers the ratchet
needs on both target and drafter sides, uniform-padding disablement
while adapting, and the standard DP/V1-runner disable guards. Pipeline
parallelism is untested upstream and in the field; that is what the
fender trial boot decides.

Off is inert: without the new fields nothing executes. Controller law
and config predicates unit-tested (7 tests); full scheduler suite green
(238).
